class:: RIRFDNModel
summary:: Prepared compact late-field model fitted from an impulse response
categories:: UGens>Reverbs, Libraries>CamaraObscura
related:: Guides/CamaraObscura, Classes/RIRFDN

description::

RIRFDNModel stores a stable late-field FDN. The bundled code::rir2fdn:: tool
detects the direct peak, selects the late response, fits broadband and
two-band Schroeder energy decays, chooses deterministic prime delays, writes
this model, renders verification audio, and produces a text report. The
pipeline is influenced by the RIR-to-FDN literature, especially DAFx-24
RIR2FDN, without incorporating its source code or neural estimators.

This model intentionally excludes direct sound and early reflections. The
closest vanilla facility is a long link::Classes/PartConv:: impulse response;
RIRFDNModel uses far less memory and permits stable decay/tone editing, but it
cannot retain the measured FIR's exact echo pattern.

classmethods::

method:: read
Read a model created by code::rir2fdn:: or code::write::.

argument:: path
Prepared text-model path, not an audio path.

method:: fromAnalysis
Alias for code::read::, emphasizing that analysis already occurred offline.

method:: synthetic
Create a deterministic model without a measured RIR.

argument:: t60Low
Low-band reverberation T60 in seconds. The renderer converts it to the
per-delay amplitude feedback gain that produces a 60 dB energy-decay curve.

argument:: t60High
High-band reverberation T60 using the same convention.

argument:: delays
Line count from 2 through 32.

argument:: sampleRate
Exact renderer sample rate.

argument:: seed
Deterministic topology seed.

instancemethods::

method:: validate
Validate metadata, topology, T60/filter data, gains, and delay limits.

method:: summary
Return model diagnostics.

method:: load
Upload the model to a mono Buffer.

method:: write
Serialize the model.

method:: free
Free the last uploaded Buffer.

method:: plotDecay
Plot line low/high T60 targets.

method:: plotResponse
Plot the same broad two-band fit used by this first model.

examples::

code::
(
var model = RIRFDNModel.synthetic(
    3.2, 1.7, 8, sampleRate: 48000, seed: 4
);
model.summary.postln;
model.plotDecay;
)
::

code::
(
var path = PathName.tmp +/+ "creative-reverbs-example.rfdn";
var model = RIRFDNModel.synthetic(
    1.4, 0.7, 6, sampleRate: 48000, seed: 12
);
var restored;
model.write(path);
restored = RIRFDNModel.read(path);
restored.summary.postln;
File.delete(path);
)
::

